WEBVTT

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:09.860
Go go Cygnus!

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.240
Go go Cygnus!

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:10.740
Go go Cygnus!

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.110
Let's go Cygnus!

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:12.740
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.280
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:13.530
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:13.910
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:14.240
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:14.860
C-y-g-n-u-s Go!

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.960
And that's the return from the kick-off.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.340
The Baltimore Cygnus are on offense at the 30 yard line.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.840
All eyes are on the quarterback, Lionel Blue.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.680
Will he lead with a run to gain a few yards?

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.140
Set.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.850
Red 2! Block star!

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:45.730
Hike!

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.780
He starts off with a pass play!

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.780
And it's caught!

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.320
A thirty yard pass!

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.450
What a great play by Lionel Blue.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.830
Truly a work of art!

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.330
This young rookie, who burst onto the scene like a meteor,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:05.580
has become the superstar of the American Pro Football League.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:04.790
Blue.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.580
Five!

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.300
Damn, he's good!

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.680
Look at those moves, Tom!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.430
Hey, Tom.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.980
That kid has totally taken your position, huh?

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.200
Look at that, Sunny.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.410
Lionel Blue is truly the American Dream.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.160
This sport is about men smashing into one another...

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.670
Two individuals going up against each other is what you truly need to move people's hearts.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.880
I see... you understand, Sunny?

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.590
Lionel Blue has the ball and he's running with it!

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.630
Ten yards!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:57.430
Twenty yards!

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.430
What amazing speed!

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.010
Will he get a touchdown?

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.470
TOUCHDOWN!

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.850
He did it!

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.980
Lionel Blue ran for a touchdown!

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.980
What's wrong?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.780
He's not getting up.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.530
Hey, you OK?

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:56.230
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:07.580
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:19.340
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:25.640
The weak person I was is no more

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:31.230
I decided to just believe

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:38.360
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.200
I go towards you

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:49.910
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:54.040
I go towards you

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.090
Blown by the wind

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.550
Oh blown

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.100
You're taking me off the Lionel Blue case?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.520
That's right.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:18.270
Even though you're an experienced detective, we don't need your help this time.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.190
But, Chief...

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.200
You're going to handle another case.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.570
Got any suspects?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.410
Only a professional...

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:34.960
and a professional among professionals at that...

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.420
would be capable of shooting a randomly moving target amidst a large crowd.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.210
Listen, Lou.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:47.350
You can't catch killers like this with old, decrepit, by-the-book techniques.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.060
We know who did it.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.100
The only thing we're doing with this case is proving it.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.110
We suspect an above first-class sniper by the name of Golgo 13.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:04.030
He was seen here in Baltimore before the game started.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.610
And where is he now?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.240
We've already taken measures.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.300
Your license.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.010
What happened?

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:39.230
Mr. Duke Tougou, you arrived in Baltimore Airport on a TW Flight today, yes?

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:39.900
Yes.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.280
We're taking you to Baltimore Hospital.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:44.900
Why?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.990
There was a cholera patient on the TW flight you boarded.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.910
We're placing you in quarantine until we can confirm that you're not infected.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:08.970
Here.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.970
This is where he was shot.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.770
What can you tell from here?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:19.560
We created a 3D model based off of this image and simulated the bullet's trajectory.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.440
From here we can figure out where the shot was fired, which is to say, the sniper's location.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:27.990
Even if you find that, what then?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:33.450
From there we pick up an image of the crowd, magnify it, and we've got our sniper.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.160
I doubt such a convenient image exists.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.620
And even if it does,

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:45.880
unless it's a fairly close-up shot, computer-enhanced images aren't admitted as evidence.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.090
Don't worry about that.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.720
The game was being recorded by a next-generation HD camera

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.760
as part of a trial run in cooperation with the manufacturer.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:59.230
The resolution on this camera is high enough to distinguish between individual seats in the stadium.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:03.230
It's a test unit though, so the only master is here.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.110
Do you understand now?

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:12.700
Traditional investigation techniques that rely on the individual's intuition aren't good enough to catch this guy.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.080
Hey, where are you going?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.580
I'm going after the Lionel Blue killer...

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.210
with those "decrepit traditional techniques" of mine.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.340
Hey, Lou, wait!

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.480
Sunny, you watch the car.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.000
What's wrong?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.870
Why won't you talk?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:09.010
I asked where you were when Lionel Blue was killed in Memorial Stadium.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.550
You arrived at the Baltimore Airport three hours before the game began.

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:20.520
From there, you went straight to your hotel, hung around for an hour, and then left.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.520
After that, you have no alibi.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.400
Listen, you killed the American Dream!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.400
You won't get away with that!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.860
That poker face of yours won't last long.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.740
Our CSI department is working on some kind of video analysis.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.040
But I'm going to get you myself.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:39.740
Just wait!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.870
It's him.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.580
He's a professional among professionals.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:52.260
Only an ice cold man like this, can accurately strike a target that's moving that erratically.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.050
It's like I'm looking at a computer.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:01.270
For such a person to be born... have the times changed that radically?

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.270
Am I behind the times now?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.610
What do the cops want to ask me?

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.410
Celebrating already?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:18.870
What?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:25.000
I'd imagine you're the happiest person in the world now that Lionel Blue's dead, Tom.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.130
You can go back to your quarterback position, yes?

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.090
Yeah...

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:32.760
Wait, are you trying to tell me I did it?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.340
Sorry, I was sitting on the bench then.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.720
You didn't have to do it yourself...

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.720
IF you hired a professional.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:50.270
One week ago, you withdrew three million dollars from your account at National Bank.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.230
What did you use it for?

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.530
I don't have to tell you.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.240
Then let's talk about something else.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:03.410
At this very moment, an Asian by the name of Golgo 13 is being held at the Baltimore Police Hospital.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:08.920
The cops think he's their man, a super high-class sniper.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:14.920
And the price of hiring him to kill someone is three million dollars.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.510
It's the same amount you withdrew from the bank.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.600
Do you intend to tell me that it's a coincidence?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.180
I don't know anything!

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.470
It has nothing to do with me!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.270
Leave!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.850
Please, leave!

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.810
I guess I'll talk to you later.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.070
Let's go, Sunny.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.530
He'll make his move.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.330
Now he'll make his move...

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.920
Did you find the sniping point?

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.750
Yes, look at this.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:11:00.470
We made a 3D model of Lionel Blue based off of his autopsy report.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.800
I'll add the impact point here.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:09.730
We put it in the stadium's CAD data and calculated the bullet's trajectory.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.230
The bullet was fired from the C3 stand,

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.900
and, even including a margin of calculation error, we can say for sure it was fired from this area.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.280
You've whittled it down, huh?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:20.950
Yes.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:25.580
Now, we just pull out the broadcast data from this area, and we can take a detailed look.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.910
It's almost time.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.160
Now the Lionel Blue case is solved!

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.670
A touchdown for the Baltimore city police!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.670
That's right.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.340
The super big shot that even the FBI couldn't catch...

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.180
the Baltimore police will make a touchdown on this!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.210
He's made his move, Sunny.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.920
Crimes are committed by humans.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.470
He has contact with Golgo 13.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.060
I won't lose to a computer.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:33.730
I'll catch the man who destroyed the American Dream myself.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.280
No.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:52.250
This isn't the way to the hospital where Golgo 13 is.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.250
Tom, where are you going?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:21.190
That mansion belongs to the football gambler, Ted O'Brian...

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.150
I see...

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:27.280
Tom hired Golgo through O'Brian...

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:32.580
Now we'll analyze each individual seat.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:37.290
We'll use chromatic analysis to determine the intermediate portions,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:45.630
that is, people who are neither Caucasian or African-American, only Asian.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.300
I see... Golgo 13 is Asian.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.060
Now we try them one by one.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.100
This is the last one.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.400
This is...

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:08.070
This is the closest we can get with this shot.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:16.000
It's likely that he pretended to be a cameraman and hid his rifle within the rangefinder.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.870
That would keep the other fans from noticing.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.710
We've got the method down.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:25.710
But we can't see the sniper's face in this shot.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:33.310
We've got every video that was recorded during the game, not just the one used for broadcasting.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.730
We've already divided them up and started to check them.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:41.980
If there's any footage of this point taken from another angle...

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:46.490
We can prove that this man is Golgo 13, right?

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.570
Hurry!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.570
Don't worry about nonsense, Tom.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.700
But Golgo 13 is in the police's hands...

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:56.830
We need to do something.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:01.250
He will never give the name of his employer, never.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.210
I promise on my life.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.840
Don't worry about him.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:24.110
What worries me more, is your mouth.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.690
From the way you're talking, the police have been after you.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:35.530
If you give him up, then I won't live long either, since I was the one who acted as the intermediary.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.040
I'll be eliminated by him.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.580
Of course, so will you.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:47.630
But I have no intention of dying with you.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.050
W-What are you doing?

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.470
W-What are you doing?

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.390
Don't move!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:13.740
Director...

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.240
Is something wrong?

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.240
Are the results from the test back yet?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.120
Just a little more.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.090
Director, what's wrong?

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.640
About that Asian... Duke Tougou...

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:41.310
I can't keep holding him here in isolation for cholera.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:46.400
Then start treating him for cholera!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.110
We can't!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.280
He knows too much
about medicine.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.110
We can't keep fooling him.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:57.530
J-Just keep him
as long as you can!

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:01.540
If you run out of ideas,
I'll send an officer over!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:03.620
Hurry!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.460
Hurry, please!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:19.850
An investigation has to begin with searching the scene of the crime for evidence.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:24.310
It's important to use human eyes and legs instead of a computer.

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:35.820
What's wrong, Sunny?

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:48.290
A 5.56 NATO round...

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:52.920
This matches the one extracted from Lionel Blue's head during the autopsy.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.170
But...

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:01.050
A professional like him leaving the spent casing behind?

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:14.440
I found it!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:17.320
Footage showing the C3 stand from another angle.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.570
OK, send it here!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.920
What's wrong, Sunny?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.590
I don't see a thing, Sunny.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.590
OK, here it is.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.760
Expanding the area around the cameraman.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.110
So it is you.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.730
What are you doing?

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.990
Shut your dog up.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.070
We've reached a critical juncture!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.740
Don't get in our way.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.990
I found who hired Golgo 13.

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.240
What?

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:11.580
The second-string quarterback, Tom Harton, and the football gambler, Ted O'Brian.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:12.420
What?

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.210
Can we get a testimony?

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.630
Both of them are dead.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.130
I killed O'Brian.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.180
What?

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:25.060
It was self-defense, but I'm prepared for my punishment.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:25.640
And this...

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.140
I found it at the stadium.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.230
This-

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.100
Where?

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.360
Where did you find this?

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.190
The C3 Stand.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:38.780
C3... I knew it.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:39.150
Chief!

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:41.150
We've got the shot.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:41.660
What?

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:43.660
Do you see him?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:43.660
Yes!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.620
Just a second...

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:48.500
We got it!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.670
W-What's wrong?

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.670
What happened?

00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.880
Look at that...

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:00.420
Huh?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:05.930
A fire has broken out... a fire has broken out.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:05.930
I saw it!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.430
I saw the guy's face clearly...

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.930
Somebody call an ambulance.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:14.900
It appears it was a highly flammable tracer bullet.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:18.150
I-It's him... Golgo 13 did it...

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.990
B-But now...

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.160
All personnel evacuate immediately.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:39.800
Director, when did he leave the hospital, and when did he come back?

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.010
Him?

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.970
He hasn't left the hospital for a second.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.140
What did you say?!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:49.560
To leave you need to go out via the hallway.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:53.310
The nurses at the nurse station would have seen him.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.980
They're on duty 24 hours a day...

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.770
And our security cameras too...

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.030
Impossible.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.740
I see...

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.860
He left from the window.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:10.370
I don't think that's possible... none of the windows in this building open enough to allow a person to leave.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:13.500
He couldn't leave without breaking it.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.370
Chief.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.000
What?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.170
He had a chance to leave if he wanted to.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:24.510
He just needed to distract the nurses for a second.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.380
The emergency exit is there.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:29.890
But the sercurity cameras?

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.470
Those cameras switch between images.

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.390
If he went through a dead spot in the rotation...

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:37.650
Chief, let's arrest him.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.110
W-We can't.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.190
Those are all assumptions!

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.530
We don't have any proof!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.990
But, Chief...

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:48.870
You know he's the guy, right?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.950
We need real proof!

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:57.580
It'd be easier to get the dead to talk than try and get him to confess!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:59.420
By the way, Director.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:03.420
How long does it take to run tests for cholera?

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:04.460
W-Well, uh...

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.170
W-Well, uh...

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:49.680
Chiisana koto ni zenryoku ni naru kimi no sugata yuuki ni natta hibi

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:49.680
Those days I saw you giving your all for small things filled me with courage

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:57.140
Zutto horyuu shippanashi jya ugokenai

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:57.140
If I keep them suspended then I won't be able to move

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:06.690
GARASU no HAIWEI ni tatteiru you ni

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:06.690
It's like I'm standing on a glass highway

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:13.910
Yume to kiken to senaka awase demo

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:13.910
Even if I'm standing back to back with dreams and danger

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:21.040
Kono nagai michi wo sukoshizutsu arukou

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:21.040
I'll take this long road one step at a time

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:27.210
Soshite kimi wa ano koro mitai ni

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:27.210
And I need you to smile

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.220
Waratteite

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.220
Like you did back then

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:36.850
Shiokaze ni yurete sasayakiatta

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:36.850
It shook in the sea breeze and whispered

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:47.440
Kagayaiteita tooi ano hi wa kagerou

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:47.440
That distant and shining day is a shimmering haze

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:49.320
The shining days

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:55.280
Tsumaranai koto ni makeru ni wa hayasugiru

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:55.280
I can't lose to something so trivial

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:05.590
Lance has taken scandal photos all over the world.

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:12.800
What he aims for as his last job, is Golgo 13 the second he fires his shot.

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:17.220
When a camera finder and rifle scope intersect...

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:19.640
Golgo's fate is decided.

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:22.730
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:26.230
Cross Angle

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:23.810
Cross Angle.

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:28.610
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
